  "grammar": [
    { "id": "roots", "title": "Roots: the same idea as Arabic", "concept": "root-pattern", "body": [
      "Hebrew words are built on 3-consonant roots, exactly like Arabic. **k-t-v** = writing: katáv (wrote), mikhtáv (letter), któvet (address). Arabic k-t-b: katab, maktūb, kitāb.",
      "**s-f-r** = book/telling/counting: séfer (book), sofér (writer), sifriyá (library), sipúr (story), mispár (number).",
      "Regular correspondences help you guess: Hebrew **sh** ↔ Arabic **s** (shalóm / salām), Hebrew **v** after a vowel ↔ Arabic **b** (katáv / katab)."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "הַסּוֹפֵר כָּתַב סֵפֶר בַּסִּפְרִיָּה.", "tr": "ha-sofér katáv séfer ba-sifriyá.", "en": "The writer wrote a book in the library." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "ro1", "prompt": "What is the root of מִכְתָּב (letter)?", "answer": "כ-ת-ב", "tr": "k-t-v" },
      { "id": "ro2", "prompt": "What is the root of סִפְרִיָּה (library)?", "answer": "ס-פ-ר", "tr": "s-f-r" },
      { "id": "ro3", "prompt": "What is the root of מַפְתֵּחַ (key)?", "answer": "פ-ת-ח", "tr": "p-t-kh" },
      { "id": "ro4", "prompt": "Which Arabic word shares the root of תַּלְמִיד?", "answer": "تلميذ", "tr": "tilmīdh" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "patterns", "title": "Patterns (mishkalim)", "concept": "root-pattern", "body": [
      "**miCCaC** often = a place or thing: mikhtáv (letter), misrád (office), mivkhán (exam), mispár (number). Compare Arabic maCCaC: maktab.",
      "**CoCeC** = the one who does it: sofér (writer), moré (teacher), shomér (guard). Arabic CāCiC: kātib.",
      "**CaCuC** = done to it: patú'akh (opened, open), katúv (written). Arabic maCCūC: maftūḥ, maktūb.",
      "**maCCeaC** = a tool: mafté'akh (key). Arabic miCCāC: miftāḥ."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "הַמַּפְתֵּחַ בַּמִּשְׂרָד, וְהַדֶּלֶת פְּתוּחָה.", "tr": "ha-mafté'akh ba-misrád, ve-ha-délet ptukhá.", "en": "The key is in the office, and the door is open." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "pa1", "prompt": "Hebrew 'writer' (from s-f-r):", "answer": "סוֹפֵר", "tr": "sofér" },
      { "id": "pa2", "prompt": "Hebrew 'letter' (from k-t-v):", "answer": "מִכְתָּב", "tr": "mikhtáv" },
      { "id": "pa3", "prompt": "Hebrew 'open' (from p-t-kh):", "answer": "פָּתוּחַ", "tr": "patú'akh" },
      { "id": "pa4", "prompt": "Hebrew 'key' (from p-t-kh):", "answer": "מַפְתֵּחַ", "tr": "mafté'akh" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "past", "title": "Past tense: endings", "concept": "aspect", "body": [
      "Past = stem + person ending: **-ti** I · **-ta** you (m) · **-t** you (f) · (none) he · **-a** she · **-nu** we · **-tem/-ten** you (pl) · **-u** they. katáv → **katávti** I wrote, **katvá** she wrote.",
      "Same shape as Arabic (katab-t, katab-na). Negate with **lo**: lo katávti."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "הָלַכְתִּי לָאוּנִיבֶרְסִיטָה וְרָאִיתִי אֶת נוֹעָה.", "tr": "halákhti la-universíta ve-ra'íti et Nóa.", "en": "I went to the university and saw Noa." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "ps1", "prompt": "Say: I went to the market yesterday.", "answer": "הָלַכְתִּי לַשּׁוּק אֶתְמוֹל.", "tr": "halákhti la-shúk etmól." },
      { "id": "ps2", "prompt": "Ask a man: What did you do today?", "answer": "מָה עָשִׂיתָ הַיּוֹם?", "tr": "ma asíta ha-yóm?" },
      { "id": "ps3", "prompt": "Say: I ate, and afterwards I slept.", "answer": "אָכַלְתִּי, וְאַחַר כָּךְ יָשַׁנְתִּי.", "tr": "akhálti, ve-akhár kakh yashánti." },
      { "id": "ps4", "prompt": "Say: I haven't finished yet.", "answer": "עוֹד לֹא גָּמַרְתִּי.", "tr": "od lo gamárti." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "haya", "title": "hayá: 'was' (and 'had')", "concept": "copula-zero", "body": [
      "The present has no 'is', but the past does: **hayíti** I was · **hayíta / hayít** you were · **hayá** he was · **haytá** she was · **hayínu** we were · **hayú** they were.",
      "'Had' = **hayá li** (there was to me): hayá li shi'úr = I had a class."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "אֶתְמוֹל הָיִיתִי בַּסִּפְרִיָּה.", "tr": "etmól hayíti ba-sifriyá.", "en": "Yesterday I was at the library." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "hy1", "prompt": "Say: I was at home.", "answer": "הָיִיתִי בַּבַּיִת.", "tr": "hayíti ba-báyit." },
      { "id": "hy2", "prompt": "Say: Yesterday I had a class.", "answer": "אֶתְמוֹל הָיָה לִי שִׁעוּר.", "tr": "etmól hayá li shi'úr." },
      { "id": "hy3", "prompt": "Say: There was no time.", "answer": "לֹא הָיָה זְמַן.", "tr": "lo hayá zman." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "shel", "title": "Whose: shel and possessive endings", "body": [
      "Everyday Hebrew says **ha-séfer shelí** = the book of mine: shelí, shelkhá, shelákh, shelό, shelá, shelánu, shelakhém, shelahém.",
      "Family words often take a short ending instead: **akhí** (my brother), **akhotí** (my sister), **bití** (my daughter): like Arabic ʔakhi, ʔukhti."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "זֹאת הַמִּשְׁפָּחָה שֶׁלִּי.", "tr": "zot ha-mishpakhá shelí.", "en": "This is my family." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "sh1", "prompt": "Say: my book", "answer": "הַסֵּפֶר שֶׁלִּי", "tr": "ha-séfer shelí" },
      { "id": "sh2", "prompt": "Say: your (m) house", "answer": "הַבַּיִת שֶׁלְּךָ", "tr": "ha-báyit shelkhá" },
      { "id": "sh3", "prompt": "Say: my sister", "answer": "אֲחוֹתִי", "tr": "akhotí" },
      { "id": "sh4", "prompt": "Say: This is Noa's house.", "answer": "זֶה הַבַּיִת שֶׁל נוֹעָה.", "tr": "ze ha-báyit shel Nóa." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "smikhut", "title": "X of Y: smikhut", "concept": "construct", "body": [
      "Two nouns side by side = 'X of Y': **bet séfer** (house of book = school), **bet kholím** (house of sick people = hospital). Just like Arabic iḍāfa (bēt Layla).",
      "The first noun changes shape and never takes ha-: báyit → **bet**; words in -a → **-at**: ugá → **ugát shokolád** (chocolate cake). 'The' goes on the second noun: **bet ha-séfer** = the school."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "אִמָּא שֶׁלִּי עוֹבֶדֶת בְּבֵית חוֹלִים.", "tr": "íma shelí ovédet be-vét kholím.", "en": "My mom works in a hospital." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "sm1", "prompt": "Say: school (house of book)", "answer": "בֵּית סֵפֶר", "tr": "bet séfer" },
      { "id": "sm2", "prompt": "Say: the school", "answer": "בֵּית הַסֵּפֶר", "tr": "bet ha-séfer" },
      { "id": "sm3", "prompt": "Say: hospital (house of the sick)", "answer": "בֵּית חוֹלִים", "tr": "bet kholím" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "numbers", "title": "Numbers 1–10", "body": [
      "Counting uses the forms you learned: **akhát, shtáyim, shalósh, árba, khámesh, shesh, shéva, shmóne, tésha, éser**. These also go with feminine nouns: shalósh she'elót.",
      "Masculine nouns take longer forms: **shloshá yeladím, arba'á sfarím**. Many Israelis mix them up in speech, so don't stress about it yet. 'Two' before a noun: **shney** (m) / **shtey** (f)."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "יֵשׁ לִי שָׁלוֹשׁ שְׁאֵלוֹת וּשְׁנֵי סְפָרִים.", "tr": "yesh li shalósh she'elót u-shné sfarím.", "en": "I have three questions and two books." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "nm1", "prompt": "Say: two coffees", "answer": "שְׁנֵי קָפֶה", "tr": "shne kafé" },
      { "id": "nm2", "prompt": "Say: It costs ten shekels.", "answer": "זֶה עוֹלֶה עֶשֶׂר שְׁקָלִים.", "tr": "ze olé éser shkalím." },
      { "id": "nm3", "prompt": "Say: It's four o'clock.", "answer": "הַשָּׁעָה אַרְבַּע.", "tr": "ha-sha'á árba." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "article", "title": "ha- 'the' and adjective agreement", "concept": "definiteness", "body": [
      "'The' is the prefix **ha-**: ha-báyit, ha-shúk. After b-, l-, k- it merges: **ba-báyit** (in the house), **la-shúk** (to the market).",
      "Adjectives copy ha-: **ha-báyit ha-gadól** = the big house. Without ha- on the adjective it's a sentence: **ha-báyit gadól** = the house is big. Exactly like Arabic il-bēt il-kbīr / il-bēt kbīr."
    ], "examples": [
      { "text": "הַשּׁוּק הַגָּדוֹל זוֹל.", "tr": "ha-shúk ha-gadól zol.", "en": "The big market is cheap." }
    ], "drills": [
      { "id": "ar1", "prompt": "Say: the big house", "answer": "הַבַּיִת הַגָּדוֹל", "tr": "ha-báyit ha-gadól" },
      { "id": "ar2", "prompt": "Say: The house is big.", "answer": "הַבַּיִת גָּדוֹל.", "tr": "ha-báyit gadól." },
      { "id": "ar3", "prompt": "Say: in the market", "answer": "בַּשּׁוּק", "tr": "ba-shúk" }
    ], "verified": false }
  ],
  "texts": [
    { "id": "d05", "title": "In the library", "level": "U5", "kind": "dialogue", "lines": [
      { "sp": "You", "text": "סְלִיחָה, הַסִּפְרִיָּה פְּתוּחָה?", "tr": "slikhá, ha-sifriyá ptukhá?", "en": "Excuse me, is the library open?" },
      { "sp": "Librarian", "text": "כֵּן, הִיא פְּתוּחָה כָּל יוֹם. מָה אַתָּה צָרִיךְ?", "tr": "ken, hi ptukhá kol yom. ma atá tsaríkh?", "en": "Yes, it's open every day. What do you need?" },
      { "sp": "You", "text": "אֲנִי רוֹצֶה סֵפֶר בְּעִבְרִית לַשִּׁעוּר.", "tr": "aní rotsé séfer be-ivrít la-shi'úr.", "en": "I want a book in Hebrew for class." },
      { "sp": "Librarian", "text": "יֵשׁ הַרְבֵּה סְפָרִים שָׁם. מִי הַמּוֹרֶה?", "tr": "yesh harbé sfarím sham. mi ha-moré?", "en": "There are lots of books there. Who's the teacher?" },
      { "sp": "You", "text": "הַמּוֹרָה מֵחֵיפָה. הִיא גַּם סוֹפֶרֶת!", "tr": "ha-morá me-kháyfa. hi gam soféret!", "en": "The teacher is from Haifa. She's also a writer!" },
      { "sp": "Librarian", "text": "יֵשׁ לְךָ מִבְחָן?", "tr": "yesh lekhá mivkhán?", "en": "Do you have an exam?" },
      { "sp": "You", "text": "כֵּן, מָחָר. וְעוֹד שְׁאֵלָה: אֵיפֹה הַמִּשְׂרָד?", "tr": "ken, makhár. ve-ód she'elá: éfo ha-misrád?", "en": "Yes, tomorrow. And another question: where's the office?" },
      { "sp": "Librarian", "text": "שָׁם. בְּהַצְלָחָה!", "tr": "sham. be-hatslakhá!", "en": "There. Good luck!" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "d06", "title": "What did you do yesterday?", "level": "U6", "kind": "dialogue", "names": ["נועה"], "lines": [
      { "sp": "Noa", "text": "מָה עָשִׂיתָ אֶתְמוֹל?", "tr": "ma asíta etmól?", "en": "What did you do yesterday?" },
      { "sp": "Venu", "text": "קַמְתִּי בַּבֹּקֶר וְהָלַכְתִּי לָאוּנִיבֶרְסִיטָה.", "tr": "kámti ba-bóker ve-halákhti la-universíta.", "en": "I got up in the morning and went to the university." },
      { "sp": "Noa", "text": "וּמָה אָכַלְתָּ?", "tr": "u-má akhálta?", "en": "And what did you eat?" },
      { "sp": "Venu", "text": "אָכַלְתִּי לֶחֶם וְשָׁתִיתִי קָפֶה. לֹא הָיָה זְמַן.", "tr": "akhálti lékhem ve-shatíti kafé. lo hayá zman.", "en": "I ate bread and drank coffee. There was no time." },
      { "sp": "Noa", "text": "וְאַחֲרֵי הַשִּׁעוּר?", "tr": "ve-akharé ha-shi'úr?", "en": "And after class?" },
      { "sp": "Venu", "text": "דִּבַּרְתִּי עִם אִמָּא, וּבָעֶרֶב לָמַדְתִּי קְצָת.", "tr": "dibárti im íma, u-va-érev lamádti ktsat.", "en": "I talked with Mom, and in the evening I studied a bit." },
      { "sp": "Noa", "text": "וְעַכְשָׁיו?", "tr": "ve-akhsháv?", "en": "And now?" },
      { "sp": "Venu", "text": "עַכְשָׁיו עוֹד יֵשׁ לִי עֲבוֹדָה. אַחַר כָּךְ לַיְלָה טוֹב!", "tr": "akhsháv od yesh li avodá. akhár kakh láyla tov!", "en": "Now I still have work. Afterwards, good night!" }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "d07", "title": "My family", "level": "U7", "kind": "reading", "names": ["חיפה"], "lines": [
      { "text": "הַמִּשְׁפָּחָה שֶׁלִּי לֹא גְּדוֹלָה.", "tr": "ha-mishpakhá shelí lo gdolá.", "en": "My family isn't big." },
      { "text": "יֵשׁ לִי אָח אֶחָד וְאָחוֹת אַחַת.", "tr": "yesh li akh ekhád ve-akhót akhát.", "en": "I have one brother and one sister." },
      { "text": "אָחִי גָּדוֹל, הוּא נָשׂוּי וְיֵשׁ לוֹ יֶלֶד קָטָן.", "tr": "akhí gadól, hu nasú'i ve-yésh lo yéled katán.", "en": "My brother is older; he's married and has a little boy." },
      { "text": "אֲחוֹתִי קְטַנָּה, הִיא בְּבֵית סֵפֶר.", "tr": "akhotí ktaná, hi be-vét séfer.", "en": "My sister is younger; she's in school." },
      { "text": "אִמָּא שֶׁלִּי רוֹפְאָה, וְאַבָּא עוֹבֵד בְּמִשְׂרָד.", "tr": "íma shelí rof'á, ve-ába ovéd be-misrád.", "en": "My mom is a doctor, and Dad works in an office." },
      { "text": "סַבָּא וְסַבְתָּא גָּרִים בְּחֵיפָה.", "tr": "sába ve-sávta garím be-kháyfa.", "en": "Grandpa and Grandma live in Haifa." },
      { "text": "אֲנִי אוֹהֵב מְאוֹד אֶת הַמִּשְׁפָּחָה שֶׁלִּי.", "tr": "aní ohév me'ód et ha-mishpakhá shelí.", "en": "I love my family very much." }
    ], "verified": false },
    { "id": "d08", "title": "At the shuk", "level": "U8", "kind": "dialogue", "lines": [
      { "sp": "You", "text": "שָׁלוֹם, כַּמָּה זֶה?", "tr": "shalóm, káma ze?", "en": "Hi, how much is this?" },
      { "sp": "Vendor", "text": "עֶשֶׂר שְׁקָלִים!", "tr": "éser shkalím!", "en": "Ten shekels!" },
      { "sp": "You", "text": "עֶשֶׂר? יָקָר מִדַּי!", "tr": "éser? yakár midáy!", "en": "Ten? Too expensive!" },
      { "sp": "Vendor", "text": "לֹא יָקָר! זֶה טוֹב מְאוֹד.", "tr": "lo yakár! ze tov me'ód.", "en": "Not expensive! It's very good." },
      { "sp": "You", "text": "אֲנִי רוֹצֶה שְׁתַּיִם. שֶׁבַע כָּל אַחַת?", "tr": "aní rotsé shtáyim. shéva kol akhát?", "en": "I want two. Seven each?" },
      { "sp": "Vendor", "text": "לֹא, תֵּשַׁע.", "tr": "lo, tésha.", "en": "No, nine." },
      { "sp": "You", "text": "טוֹב, שְׁמוֹנֶה?", "tr": "tov, shmóne?", "en": "OK, eight?" },
      { "sp": "Vendor", "text": "יַאללָה, בְּסֵדֶר. רַק בִּשְׁבִילְךָ!", "tr": "yálla, be-séder. rak bishvilkhá!", "en": "Yalla, OK. Only for you!" },
      { "sp": "You", "text": "תּוֹדָה רַבָּה!", "tr": "todá rabá!", "en": "Thanks a lot!" }
    ], "verified": false }
  ]
